hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19085","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Ubayd Allah who said: Haddathani Said ibn Abi Said from Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from his father that Ammar prayed two rakas. Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, I do not see but that you have lightened them. He said: Did I omit anything of their limits? He said: No, but you lightened them. He said: I hastened with them against forgetfulness. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man may pray, and perhaps there is for him of his prayer naught but a tenth of it, a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, till he ended to the last of the number."
"19086","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abi al-Bakhtari who said: Ammar said on the day of Siffin: Bring me a drink of milk, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last drink you drink in this world is a drink of milk. So he was brought a drink of milk, drank it, then advanced and was killed."
"19087","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Ziyad Abu Umar from al-Hasan from Ammar ibn Yasir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my umma is like rain: it is not known whether its first is better or its last."
"19088","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Sufyan from Salama, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, from Abi Malik and Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza who said: We were with Umar when a man came to him saying: O Commander of the Faithful, we stay a month and two months finding no water. Umar said: As for me, I would not pray till I find water. Ammar said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you remember where we were in such-and-such place pasturing camels, and you know that we became junub? He said: Yes. He said: I rolled in the dust, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, and he laughed and said: Pure earth would have sufficed you. And he struck the earth with his palms, then blew into them, then wiped with them his face and part of his forearms. He said: Fear Allah, O Ammar. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you wish I shall not mention it as long as I live. He said: Nay, by Allah, but we entrust you with what you have taken charge of."
"19089","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Habib from Abi al-Bukhturi that Ammar ibn Yasir was brought a drink of milk, so he laughed. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last drink I drink is milk, till I die."
"19090","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Amr ibn Murra who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Salama say: I saw Ammar on the day of Siffin, an old man, large, dark, tall, holding the spear in his hand, his hand trembling. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I have fought with this banner with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times, and this is the fourth. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, though they strike us till they bring us to the mountain tops of Hajar, I would know that our righteous ones are upon the truth and that they are upon misguidance."
"19091","Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba - and Hajjaj said: Haddathani Shuba - who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Abi Nadra - Hajjaj said: I heard Aba Nadra - from Qays ibn Abbad who said: I said to Ammar: Do you see your fighting - Hajjaj said: Do you see this matter, meaning their fighting - a judgment you have judged? Hajjaj said: Do you see this matter, meaning their fighting, a judgment you have judged? For judgment errs and hits right, or a covenant covenanted to you by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to us nothing he did not covenant to people generally. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in my umma - Shuba said: And I think he said: Haddathani Hudhayfa: Indeed in my umma are twelve hypocrites. He said: They shall not enter Paradise nor find its scent till the camel passes through the eye of the needle. Eight of them, the dubayla suffices them - a lamp of fire appearing in their shoulders till it rises in their chests."
"19092","Haddathana Bahz ibn Asad, haddathana Hammad ibn Salama, akhbarana Ata al-Khurasani from Yahya ibn Yamar that Ammar said: I came to my family at night, my hands cracked, so they perfumed me with saffron. I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), greeted him, but he did not return upon me nor welcome me, saying: Wash this. He said: I went and washed it, then came, some of it remaining upon me, greeted him, but he did not return upon me nor welcome me, saying: Wash this from you. I went and washed it, then came, greeted him, so he returned upon me and welcomed me, saying: The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever, nor one perfumed with saffron, nor one junub. And he permitted the junub, when he sleeps or eats or drinks, to perform wudu."
"19093","Haddathana Bahz, haddathana Shuba, haddathana al-Hakam from Dharr from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father that a man asked Umar ibn al-Khattab about tayammum, and he did not know what to say. Ammar ibn Yasir said: Do you not remember where we were in an expedition, and I became junub and rolled in the dust, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This would have sufficed you thus. And Shuba struck his hands upon his knees and blew into his hands, then wiped with them his face and his palms, once."
"19094","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Ammar ibn Yasir Abi al-Yaqzan who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the necklace of Aisha perished, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed till dawn lit, and Abu Bakr was angry with Aisha. Then the concession was revealed upon them for wiping with the dusty ground. Abu Bakr entered upon her saying: You are indeed blessed; a concession has been revealed concerning you. So we struck with our hands to our faces, and struck with our hands a strike to the shoulders and armpits."
"19095","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana al-Ala ibn Salih from Adi ibn Thabit: Thana Abu Rashid who said: Ammar ibn Yasir addressed us, being brief in his address. A man from Quraysh said to him: You have spoken healing speech; would that you had lengthened. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to lengthen the address."
"19096","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Ibn Jurayj - and Rawh: Haddathana Ibn Jurayj: Akhbarani Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khawwar that he heard Yahya ibn Yamar informing from a man who informed him from Ammar ibn Yasir - Umar claimed that Yahya had named that man, and Umar forgot him - that Ammar said: I perfumed myself with khaluq, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he rebuked me, saying: Go, O son of Umm Ammar, and wash it from you. I returned and washed it from me. He said: Then I returned to him, and he rebuked me also, saying: Return and wash it from you - mentioning three times."
"19097","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, haddathana Mamar from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba that Ammar ibn Yasir used to narrate that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a journey, with him Aisha, and her necklace perished. People were detained seeking it till they woke with no water with them. Then tayammum was revealed. Ammar said: They stood and wiped with them: they struck their hands and wiped their faces, then returned and struck with their hands a second time, then wiped their hands to the armpits - or he said: to the shoulders."
"19098","Haddathana Sufyan from Amr from Ata from Aish ibn Anas, he heard it from Ali, meaning upon the minbar of Kufa: I used to find madhy, and I was shy to ask him, as his daughter was with me. So I said to Ammar: Ask him. So he asked him, and he said: Wudu suffices for it."
"19099","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar who said: Thana Yunus from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba that Ammar ibn Yasir used to narrate that the concession which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning the dusty ground - then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: They struck their palms in the dusty ground and wiped with them their faces one wipe, then returned and struck and wiped their hands to the shoulders and armpits."
"19100","Haddathana Safwan ibn Isa, akhbarana Ibn Ajlan from Said al-Maqburi from Umar ibn al-Hakam from Abd Allah ibn Anama who said: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir enter the mosque and pray, lightening the prayer. He said: When he went out I stood to him saying: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you have lightened. He said: Did you see me omit anything of its limits? I said: No. He said: I hastened with it against the lapse of Satan. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The servant may pray prayer, and there is written for him of it naught but a tenth of it, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, a fourth, a third, a half."
